# CSS Architecture

## The three layers

### 1. `app/globals.css` — truly global only

Lives here if it's used in 3+ places across different directories, or is a foundation primitive.

- `:root` design tokens (colors, spacing, type scale, radius, line-height, tracking)
- `@layer base` — html, body, scrollbar
- Layout primitives: `.page-shell`, `.layout-grid`, `.hero-gap`, `.text-column`, `.with-sidebar`
- Type scale: all `.type-*` classes
- Universal surfaces: `.card`, `.card-tinted`, `.card-tinted-inner`, `.card-cta`, `.panel`, `.link-pill`
- Stack utilities: `.stack-xs` through `.stack-5xl`
- Keyframes used by Tailwind animation tokens

**Do not add** component-specific styles here. If you're adding a class used in only one component,
it belongs in a CSS Module.

### 2. CSS Modules (`.module.css`) — component-specific

Use when a component needs styles that can't be cleanly expressed as Tailwind utilities
(pseudo-elements, complex selectors, `::before`/`::after` with dynamic vars).

Co-locate next to the component file:
```
components/projects/ProjectCard.tsx
components/projects/ProjectCard.module.css   ← scoped styles
```

Rules for modules:
- Use CSS custom properties (`var(--color-border)`) — they're globally available
- Do NOT use `@apply` in CSS Modules
- Keep the scope tight — only styles for that one component
- Keyframes used by only one component belong here, not in globals

Current modules: `ProjectCard.module.css`, `ChatAnimation.module.css`, `page.module.css` (project slug page)

### 3. Inline Tailwind — single-property constraints and layout

Use for layout constraints, responsive modifiers, and one-off overrides that don't need a class.

```tsx
// ✅ Fine as inline Tailwind (single layout constraint)
<p className="type-h4 max-w-[420px]">

// ✅ Fine as inline Tailwind (responsive layout)
<div className="col-span-12 md:col-span-6">

// ❌ Not fine — this is a multi-property visual pattern, use globals or a module
<div className="flex flex-col gap-6 p-6 rounded-[20px] border border-[#272921] bg-[#151310]">
```

## Decision tree

```
Does it use design tokens and appear in 3+ places across different directories?
  → globals.css (@layer components)

Is it a complex visual pattern for a single component (pseudo-elements, etc.)?
  → CSS Module

Is it a single layout value (max-width, col-span, order)?
  → Inline Tailwind

Is it a typography/color/spacing utility?
  → Use existing type-*, color-*, space-* Tailwind utilities (never recreate them)
```

## What NOT to do

```tsx
// ❌ Hardcoded hex in className
className="text-[#A39E8E] bg-[#23221b]"

// ❌ Hardcoded px size for type
className="text-[14px] leading-[1.45]"

// ❌ Arbitrary spacing that has a token equivalent
className="gap-[20px] p-[24px]"    // use gap-lg p-xl

// ❌ Adding a global CSS class for something used in one place
// (add to CSS module or compose inline instead)
```
